# --- Internal dev task files (contain debugging context, never commit ---
.brain/cc_tasks/
docs/reports/

# --- Timestamped provider-migration backups --------------------------------
# Auto-generated when a provider is added/removed (e.g.
# config.yaml.opencode_zen.20260805-000746.bak). These accumulate over time and
# contain live API keys, so they must never be committed.
*.[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9].bak
.brain/CHANGELOG.md

# --- Local test assets & runtime data (never commit) ---
test-assets/
data/

# --- .brain runtime debris & live-token artifacts (2026-09-08 hygiene sweep) ---
# Logs dir holds router lockfiles + session-token JSONs; backups dir
# holds timestamped config.yaml copies WITH LIVE API KEYS; *.json census/scan
# outputs and forensic diffs are session-local. Token files must NEVER be
# tracked. (Already-tracked .brain files are unaffected by ignore rules.)
.brain/logs/
.brain/backups/
.brain/scripts/
.brain/qwen_*.tok
.brain/qwen_*.tok.json
.brain/*.json
.brain/*.diff
.brain/*.txt
.brain/*.bak
.brain/vulture_*.txt

# --- Local MCP config (machine-specific paths, never commit) ---
# .mcp.json holds absolute local tooling and project paths that vary per
# machine. Ship a template instead; each dev copies .mcp.json.example -> .mcp.json
# with their own local paths. Mirrors the config.yaml / config.example.yaml pattern.
.mcp.json

